+/// Every game stamps its player's moves with its own network clock, and shows the other players
+/// at "its clock minus a short buffer". The game server set all clocks equal (message 0x39); with
+/// no server each game's clock starts when that game joined, so they differ by up to seconds, and
+/// the game whose clock is behind shows everybody else that much late. The emulators tell each
+/// other their clocks once a second and a game that is behind moves its clock forward to the one
+/// furthest ahead. (Never back: the others would drop our moves as too old.)
+/// The final (last phase) gives every player a start point around the picked place. The server
+/// sent one list; here every game builds its own (the offline setup), in its own player order,
+/// and the games overwrite each other's entries with their start-point messages, so now and then
+/// two players are put on one point. The games do not always know the same points, so nothing
+/// is decided up front: every game notes the points that show up in its list during the
+/// intermission, and in the first seconds of the final a player that stands on the same point
+/// as a player with a lower number steps to a point nobody stands on. The game's own points
+/// are 0.8 m apart (players start side by side), so "the same point" means under 0.4 m.
+/// The simulation's start, done from outside on a game that does not run it: the kin-circle lists
+/// (kinds 0x1B..0x1D) become the previous-round lists, and with `all` every list is emptied.
+void Assist::State::MapClearLists(u64 map_system, bool all) {
+    for (u64 i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
+        const u64 current = map_system + MAP_LISTS + (0x1B + i) * 0x20;
+        const u64 previous = map_system + MAP_PREVIOUS + i * 0x20;
+        std::array<u64, 3> now_list{};
+        std::array<u64, 3> old_list{};
+        if (!Read(current, now_list.data(), sizeof(now_list)) ||
+            !Read(previous, old_list.data(), sizeof(old_list))) {
+            return;
+        }
+        old_list[1] = old_list[0];
+        Write(current, old_list.data(), sizeof(old_list));
+        Write(previous, now_list.data(), sizeof(now_list));
+    }
+    for (u64 kind = 0; all && kind < 0x1B; ++kind) {
+        const u64 list = map_system + MAP_LISTS + kind * 0x20;
+        Put<u64>(list + 8, Get<u64>(list));
+    }
+}
