+// offset in both load passes and adds nothing (warning) if it differs, so records can rely on it.
+// Records stay main-relative: built-in records marked executable_padding may target
+// [kDuskCaveRegionOffset, kDuskCaveRegionOffset + kDuskCaveRegionSize) if the bytes there are zero.
+// main's PatchNSO buffer is extended (zeros) up to the region end so such records fit; the loader
+// carries the region's patched bytes over to sdk's image.
+// Permission (experiment E1): the whole region is mapped plain READ (state Code), not R-X, so the
+// guest rtld's svcQueryMemory module scan (Code + R-X = module) does not see a fake module. The JIT
+// executes it anyway (MemoryReadCode checks mapping only). This is emulator-only: on hardware (or
+// NCE, where the region is disabled) execution there would fault. Code that patches the region at
+// run time must call Core::InvalidateInstructionCacheRange after writing, as for main's text.
+//
