+//  * Plain B/BL (+-128 MB) reach the region only from hook sites in main text at
+//    >= main+0x4510000 (>= main+0x4500004 for the region's first word); text ends at
+//    main+0x492AD90. Returning from the region to ANY main text address needs the same reach, so
+//    a region stub returning below main+0x4510000 must also use an absolute (ADRP) branch.
+//  * Every other hook site needs a veneer AT the hook site (main's text-end padding is full, so a
+//    single `b` to a nearby trampoline is impossible). Standard 4-word form, overwriting 4
+//    original instructions (relocate them into the region stub; none may be PC-relative unless
+//    re-encoded there, and no other code may branch into words 2-4):
+//        adrp x16, region_page          ; ADRP reach +-4 GB, always fine here
+//        add  x16, x16, #region_lo12
+//        br   x16                       ; or blr x16 for a call (clobbers x30!)
+//        <4th word: nop, or the first relocated instruction executed on return>
+//    x16/x17 (IP0/IP1) are the AAPCS64 intra-procedure scratch registers: free at function
+//    entry, right after a BL returns, and anywhere the disassembly shows them dead (written
+//    before read on every path). NOT free between a veneer/PLT load and its use, or when the
+//    function itself uses them as temporaries across the hook; check the site, else spill.
